David Justiss wrote:
>
>  - trap doors separate me from my pet

Your motivation is to find the up stairs and return to the starting
level as soon as possible.  Don't give in to the temptation to
explore as you go unless you want to face a hostile former pet.

>  - my pet eats while I'm getting killed  (I write Elbereth but it's just
> not very reliable when written in the dust)

Use missiles and the E-word lasts longer.  This is why pets may
be nice but they can't be depended upon.

>  - my pet just doesn't always attack the monsters that are attacking me
> (even when he's not eating)

Pets will only attack monsters they think they can kill.
If your pet won't go after it, neither should you.

>  - my pet keeps getting himself killed by the watch captain

Pets take the monster's level into account but not the monster's
weapons.  Watch captain is often the first monster encountered
that is strong enough to survive significant combat and also to
have a very good weapon - long sword or silver saber.

Either exit the mine town sooner of use the mine town to trim
your herd of pets.

> Nethack is frustrating.

The only possible way to stay interesting for over a decade.



